\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Does there exist an infinite group with a free probability-measure-preserving action $\Gamma\curvearrowright(X,\mu)$ such that $\beta_1^{(2)}(\Gamma)<\operatorname{cost}(R_{\Gamma\curvearrowright(X,\mu)})-1$?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2010/40}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Does there exist an infinite group with a free probability-measure-preserving action $\Gamma\curvearrowright(X,\mu)$ such that $\beta_1^{(2)}(\Gamma)<\operatorname{cost}(R_{\Gamma\curvearrowright(X,\mu)})-1$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30001578 (OWR-4428-003). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2010/40}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:30001578}

